.TH FERMI_SSO_JAR_TUI 1 "2026-10-30" "requests-fermi-sso 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fermi_sso_jar_tui \- terminal viewer for the Fermilab SSO cookie jar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fermi_sso_jar_tui
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fermi_sso_jar_tui
is a curses front end to the engine behind
.BR fermi_sso_jar (1).
The top pane lists the identity provider and every catalog site with the
state of its cookies in the jar, coloured live (green), soon (yellow),
session (cyan), expired (red) or absent (magenta); the bottom pane shows
the cookies of the selected row with their expiry and flags, values
masked. Keys prime, refresh, verify and clear through the same
.BR JarManager ,
so anything the command line can do the viewer can too.
.PP
Network work runs in a daemon thread and the screen keeps updating while
it is in flight; results arrive on the status line. The jar is re\-read
every five seconds, so a login performed by another process (the probe, a
script, the Qt viewer) shows up without a keypress.
.PP
A prime or refresh that needs a password asks for it on the bottom line.
The password is kept for the rest of the run only; the jar, not the
password, is what persists.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR "up/down" ", " j / k
Select a site.
.TP
.B enter
Toggle the cookie detail pane.
.TP
.B p
Prime the selected site: log in if its cookies do not sign in, save the jar.
.TP
.B P
Prime every site, in sequence through one identity\-provider session.
.TP
.B R
Refresh: prime only the sites that are absent, expired or expiring soon.
.TP
.B v
Verify the selected site, cookies only, against the network.
.TP
.B V
Verify every site.
.TP
.B c
Clear the selected site's cookies from the jar (asks first). On the
.B idp
row, clears the identity provider's cookies.
.TP
.B x
Purge expired cookies.
.TP
.B s
Show or mask cookie values. They are bearer credentials.
.TP
.B r
Re\-read the jar now.
.TP
.B ?
Help.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH OPTIONS
The common and credential options of
.BR fermi_sso_jar (1):
.BI \-c " FILE" ,
.BI \-\-cookie\-format " FORMAT" ,
.BI \-e " FILE" ,
.BR \-\-no\-env\-file ,
.BI \-S " FILE" ,
.BR \-\-no\-builtin\-sites ,
.BI \-\-margin " SECONDS" ,
.BI \-\-idp\-host " HOST" ,
.BI \-u " USER" ,
.BI \-\-password\-env " NAME" ,
.BI \-a " METHOD" ,
.BI \-\-pin\-source " FILE" ,
.BR \-n ,
.BR \-\-no\-save\-cookies ,
.BR \-V .
Settings resolve as there: commandline, environment, env file, catalog
settings, defaults.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on quit; 2 when standard output is not a terminal or a setting is
invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
fermi_sso_jar_tui
fermi_sso_jar_tui \-c ~/work/other.cookies \-a kerberos
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fermi_sso_jar (1),
.BR fermi_sso_jar_gui (1),
.BR fermi_sso_sites (5),
.BR fermi_sso_cookies (1)
